From b6da6516fba408951e6aa65d6cec6ac0890c9a29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:52:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] audio, windowing/gbm: only the display in use is lit, and its
 sound stays with it

With three displays on an RTX 4080 SUPER (an LG C5 with a sound bar on its
eARC, a Samsung Odyssey, an LG UltraGear), the audio setting named
hdmi:CARD=NVidia,DEV=0. The NVIDIA driver numbers its HDMI PCMs by the order
in which the displays came, not by connector: that day DEV=0 was the Odyssey.
Its output was kept on "for the sound in use" and lit again at the return
from each video, the sound went to the Odyssey for about two seconds each
time it came back, and "The sound of ... comes back" was shown at every
start. The user's decision: only the display in use is lit, unless he
chooses another display, and the sound stays where the picture is.

- The engine keeps, for each device setting, the display it was chosen with
  (audiooutput.hadesdevicedisplay, audiooutput.hadespassthroughdisplay; the
  ELD's maker, product and name), taken the first time the output names a
  display, so that a setting saved as a number moves over without asking.
  ActiveAE::INTERNAL::OutputForDisplayInUse() then decides before
  FollowedDisplayOutput(): the output that has the remembered display now,
  whatever its number, where that display is the one in use; else, as only
  the display in use is lit, the output of the display in use in place of an
  output of another display. Nothing is decided where the display in use is
  not known, has no output of its own (a monitor without audio), or has two
  outputs (two displays of one model), nor for analogue, S/PDIF or USB
  outputs; the instant of a mode change keeps the output followed to, as
  before. The setting itself is never changed; kodi.log says each change once.
- A new Expert setting, System > Audio > "Keep the display of the audio
  output on" (audiooutput.hadeslightforsound, off), keeps what was there: an
  AV receiver or sound bar on its own output of the card is kept lit, black,
  for its sound, and the remembered display's output is used whatever its
  number. Off, KEEP_OUTPUTS::OutputsForSound() keeps nothing on for any
  sound, not even the output with the picture (on anyway), so a move of Kodi
  to another display leaves nothing lit behind; what would have been kept is
  logged once, with a line that names every output that could carry sound
  with its own display (the check of each connector's own EDID, aefdb15).
  A change of the setting moves the generation of CSoundOutputsInUse
  (Touch()), so the windowing system decides again at its next commit
  without reading the setting at each one.
- The notification "The sound of ... comes back" is shown once per output in
  a run (QueueSoundBringBack()); the log says each time.
- The published identity of "the audio output of the settings" is the
  remembered display, so that with the Expert setting on, the display the
  user chose is the one lit, not the display its number has today.

Strings: core #41852/#41853, Estuary #32952/#32953 (en_gb; es_es, es_ar,
es_mx).

Tests: TestActiveAEFollowDisplay gains six tests (the three displays, a
number that is another display today, a receiver with the Expert setting on
and off, one display, what is not decided, the text of a remembered
display), run on the host with a gtest shim: 32 tests, 135 checks pass, and
six mutations (no decision by the displays, which is the behaviour before;
no display in use; no remembered display; the Expert setting ignored; two
outputs taken as one; the text's space) each fail them. A host test of
OutputsForSound() (the three displays, a receiver, one display, the engine
silent; on and off) passes 28 checks and fails with the Expert setting
ignored (the behaviour before), with the picture output kept, and without
the line of the outputs. Compiled with the compile commands of the build.
Not tried on hardware.
